# Configuration reference for the Binder Selection Agent.
#
# IMPORTANT: this app reads plain process environment variables. It does NOT
# auto-load a .env file (python-dotenv is installed but nothing calls
# load_dotenv()). Copy this file to .env for your own notes, or set the
# variables in PowerShell before starting the server:
#
#   $env:BSA_SESSION_KEY = 'paste-a-long-random-string'
#   .\scripts\run.ps1
#
# Everything except BSA_SESSION_KEY is optional; the no-config fallback is
# noted per variable.
#
# See docs/RECREATE.md for the full runbook.

# --- Sessions ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Signing key for the session cookie. If unset, the app auto-creates
# data/secret.key on first boot. Set this instead when you want the key to
# survive a data/ wipe, or when several instances must share sessions.
# BSA_SESSION_KEY=

# --- Storage ----------------------------------------------------------------
# SQLAlchemy URL. Default: sqlite:///data/prod.sqlite3 (file auto-created).
# Postgres works without code changes:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://user:pass@host:5432/binder

# LangGraph checkpointer for the engine loop. Unset -> local .checkpoints.sqlite.
# BINDER_PG_CONN=postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/binder

# --- Mail -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unset -> every message is written to data/outbox/ as a readable .txt file.
# SMTP_HOST=
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASS=
# SMTP_FROM=binder-agent@local

# --- Extraction (optional; stub runs keyless) -------------------------------
# Unset -> deterministic stub extractor. Set one provider to read genuinely
# unstructured documents with an LLM. A model may read and explain, never decide.
# APP_DEFAULT_LLM=
# NVIDIA_API_KEY=
# NVIDIA_MODEL=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY_FILE=C:\path\to\key.txt   (preferred over GEMINI_API_KEY)
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite
